(()=>{
 const {topics}=Curriculum,esc=M.esc;
 const lesson=(title,why,equations,notes)=>`<article class="panel"><div class="panel-heading"><h2>${title}</h2></div><p>${why}</p>${equations.map(e=>'<div class="math">'+e+'</div>').join('')}<p>${notes}</p></article>`;
 const fraction=(a,b)=>`<math><mfrac><mtext>${a}</mtext><mtext>${b}</mtext></mfrac></math>`;
 const content={
 systems:lesson('Preserve both force and rotation','An equivalent system must have the <strong>same total force and the same moment about a reference point</strong>. Moving a force sideways requires a couple.',['R = ΣF','M<sub>O</sub> = Σ(r<sub>Oi</sub> × F<sub>i</sub>) + ΣC<sub>i</sub>'],'Choose O first. Each position vector begins at O and ends on that force’s line of action. <strong>Applied couples are added directly.</strong> Moving along a force’s own line needs no added couple. These equivalences describe external effects on a rigid body.'),
 location:lesson('Where should the resultant act?','After adding forces and moments, find a location where the resultant reproduces the original moment.',['r × R = M<sub>O</sub>','For an intersection with y = 0: xR<sub>y</sub> = M<sub>z</sub>',fraction('M_z','R_y')+' = x'],'Divide only when <strong>Rᵧ ≠ 0</strong>. In general 3D a single force is possible only when R is nonzero and <strong>R · M = 0</strong>. If R = 0 and M ≠ 0, the system is a pure couple; if both vanish, the system is equivalent to zero external loading.'),
 distributed:lesson('A distributed load becomes a force at its centroid','The load diagram gives <strong>intensity w(x), in N/m</strong>. Its area is a force, and its first moment determines location.',['F<sub>R</sub> = ∫ w(x) dx','Q = ∫ x w(x) dx','x̄ = '+fraction('∫ x w(x) dx','∫ w(x) dx')],'Uniform load: FR = wL at L/2. Increasing triangular load: FR = wmax L/2 at <strong>2L/3 from its zero end</strong>. Split a trapezoid into a rectangle and triangle, then use x̄ = Σ(Fi xi)/ΣFi. For pressure p(x) uniform across width b, <strong>w(x) = p(x)b</strong>. If signed loads cancel to zero force, do not divide by zero; retain the remaining couple.'),
 integrals:lesson('Integration adds many small contributions','A tiny beam segment dx carries <strong>dF = w(x) dx</strong>. Summing these contributions continuously is integration.',['F<sub>R</sub> = ∫<sub>a</sub><sup>b</sup> w(x) dx','∫ c xⁿ dx = '+fraction('c xⁿ⁺¹','n + 1')+' + C, n ≠ −1','∫<sub>a</sub><sup>b</sup> w(x) dx = W(b) − W(a)'],'The bounds a and b are positions, not force values. <strong>Evaluate the upper bound minus the lower bound.</strong> N/m × m gives N; multiplying by x adds metres and produces N·m. The integration constant cancels in a definite integral. The first moment Q is not a force: dividing Q by FR gives the location in metres.')
 };
 content.systems+=lesson('Changing the reduction point','A change of reference changes the moment of the resultant force, while the force stays the same.',['M<sub>B</sub> = M<sub>O</sub> + r<sub>BO</sub> × R'],'The displacement in this formula starts at the new reference B and ends at the old reference O. Check this order before crossing.');
 content.location+=lesson('Concurrent, coplanar and parallel systems','Concurrent force lines pass through one point. Coplanar loads share a plane. Parallel loads share a direction.',['In the xy plane: M<sub>z</sub> = xR<sub>y</sub> − yR<sub>x</sub>'],'For parallel upward loads on a slab, Rz = ΣFz, Mx = Σ(y Fz), My = −Σ(x Fz). Thus x = −My/Rz and y = Mx/Rz, when Rz ≠ 0. A resultant may fall outside the body when loads oppose each other.');
 const momentExtra=lesson('Principle of moments · Varignon’s theorem','The moment of a force equals the sum of moments of its components. Choose the easier geometry; both routes must agree.',['M<sub>O</sub> = r × F = r × (F<sub>x</sub>i) + r × (F<sub>y</sub>j) + r × (F<sub>z</sub>k)','In 2D: M<sub>z</sub> = r<sub>x</sub>F<sub>y</sub> − r<sub>y</sub>F<sub>x</sub>'],'For r = (2,1,0) m and F = (30,40,0) N, Mz = 2(40) − 1(30) = +50 N·m. The alternative is magnitude F times the true perpendicular distance to its line of action.');
 const detExtra=lesson('Why the determinant has + − +','Expand the first row of the determinant with rows (i,j,k), (rx,ry,rz), and (Fx,Fy,Fz). Each 2×2 minor is ad − bc.',['M = i(ry Fz − rz Fy) − j(rx Fz − rz Fx) + k(rx Fy − ry Fx)','|A × B| = |A||B| sin θ; A × B = −B × A'],'The minus before the j minor is essential. At 0° or 180° the cross product is zero; at 90° its magnitude is largest for fixed vector lengths. A dot product produces a scalar; a cross product produces a vector perpendicular to both inputs.');
 $('moment').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',momentExtra+detExtra);
 $('axisWorkspace').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',lesson('When axis moment vanishes','The scalar triple product extracts only twist about the selected positive axis.',['M<sub>a</sub> = u<sub>a</sub> · (r × F)'],'A force parallel to the axis, or whose line of action intersects it, produces zero moment about that axis. A nonzero point moment can still have zero component along the axis.'));
 $('coupleWorkspace').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',lesson('Recognize and combine couples','A couple requires <strong>equal, opposite, parallel forces on distinct lines</strong>. Forces on the same line cancel without a couple.',['C<sub>R</sub> = ΣC<sub>i</sub>'],'Equivalent couples have identical moment vectors. You can relocate a couple on a rigid body without changing its external effect. Opposite couples can cancel even when their force-pair geometry differs.'));
 $('reference').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',lesson('Chapter 3 · system reduction and distributed loads','Match both force and moment when replacing a loading system.',['R = ΣF; MO = Σ(r × F) + ΣC','FR = ∫ w(x) dx; Q = ∫ x w(x) dx; x̄ = '+fraction('Q','FR')],'For x̄, the force denominator must be nonzero. Use common length and force units. Pressure p (N/m²) times width b (m) gives line load w (N/m). A zero-force, nonzero-moment system is a pure couple.'));
 for(const id of Object.keys(content)){
  const section=document.createElement('section');section.id=id+'Workspace';section.className='view';section.hidden=true;
  section.innerHTML=content[id]+`<article class="panel"><div class="panel-heading"><h2>${id==='integrals'?'Explore accumulated load':'Live load reduction lab'}</h2></div><p>Adjust the values. This lab uses upward force as positive and +z as counterclockwise.</p><div class="position-answer-grid"><label>Length L (m)<input id="${id}Length" type="number" min="0.01" value="4" step="any"></label><label>${id==='systems'||id==='location'?'Each force (N)':'Peak intensity (N/m)'}<input id="${id}Load" type="number" value="120" step="any"></label><label>${id==='systems'?'Applied couple (N·m)':'Load shape'}${id==='systems'?`<input id="${id}Shape" type="number" value="30" step="any">`:`<select id="${id}Shape"><option value="0">${id==='location'?'Two equal point forces':'Uniform'}</option>${id==='location'?'':'<option value="1">Increasing triangle</option><option value="2">Quadratic</option>'}</select>`}</label></div><div id="${id}Live"></div><button id="${id}Walk">Practise step by step →</button></article>`;
  document.querySelector('main').appendChild(section);
  const update=()=>{const L=Number($(id+'Length').value),w=Number($(id+'Load').value),power=Number($(id+'Shape').value);if(!Number.isFinite(L)||L<=0||!Number.isFinite(w)||!Number.isFinite(power)){ $(id+'Live').textContent='Enter a positive length and finite load values.';return;}const system=id==='systems',location=id==='location',force=system?w:location?2*w:w*L/(power+1),x=system?L:location?L/2:L*(power+1)/(power+2),moment=system?L*w+power:force*x,fmt=n=>Number(n.toPrecision(6));let shape='';for(let i=0;i<40;i++){if(location&&i!==10&&i!==29)continue;const t=location?(i===10?.25:.75):i/39,px=60+480*t,h=system?0:90*(power===0?1:t**power)*Math.sign(w);shape+=`<line x1="${px}" y1="160" x2="${px}" y2="${160-h}" stroke="#8cbcff" stroke-width="2"/>`;}$(id+'Live').innerHTML=`<svg viewBox="0 0 600 220" role="img" aria-label="Load extent and equivalent force location"><path d="M60 160H540" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="3"/>${shape}<path d="M${60+480*x/L} 160v${force<0?50:-50}" stroke="#b8f477" stroke-width="5"/><text x="60" y="195" fill="#ced9e6">0 m</text><text x="480" y="195" fill="#ced9e6">${fmt(L)} m</text><text x="65" y="28" fill="#b8f477">R = ${fmt(force)} N; x = ${fmt(x)} m</text></svg><p class="diagram-help">Horizontal extent is 0 to L metres. Load heights are normalized; arrow lengths illustrate direction, not force magnitude. Read physical values from the inputs and results.</p><div class="insight"><p><strong>Resultant:</strong> ${fmt(force)} N · <strong>Moment about O:</strong> ${fmt(moment)} N·m</p><p>${system?'R = F; MO = LF + C = '+fmt(L*w)+' + '+fmt(power):location?'R = F + F; MO = F(L/4) + F(3L/4); x = MO/R':'R = wmax L/(n+1); Q = wmax L²/(n+2); x̄ = Q/R'}</p>${!system&&w===0?'<p>Zero loading: there is no unique resultant location. The displayed x is the limiting centroid of this shape.</p>':''}</div>`;};['Length','Load','Shape'].forEach(s=>$(id+s).addEventListener('input',update));$(id+'Walk').onclick=()=>GuidedRoadmap.open(id);update();
 }
 // Group the existing entry points without changing their destinations.
 const nav=document.querySelector('nav');for(const [folderId,roadmap] of [['workspaceFolder',false],['roadmapFolder',true]]){const folder=$(folderId),children=folder.querySelector('.nav-children');children.innerHTML=[2,3].map(ch=>`<details id="${folderId}Chapter${ch}" open><summary>Chapter ${ch} · ${ch===2?'Force vectors':'Force system resultants'}</summary><div class="nav-children">${topics.filter(t=>t.chapter===ch).map(t=>`<button ${roadmap?'data-roadmap-topic="'+t.id+'"':'data-view="'+t.workspace+'"'}>${t.title}</button>`).join('')}</div></details>`).join('');if(roadmap)folder.querySelector('summary').textContent='Solid Mechanics Roadmap';}
 nav.querySelectorAll('[data-view]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>showView(b.dataset.view));nav.querySelectorAll('[data-roadmap-topic]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>GuidedRoadmap.open(b.dataset.roadmapTopic));
 const button=document.createElement('button');button.textContent='Your learning progress';button.dataset.view='mastery';button.onclick=()=>showView('mastery');nav.appendChild(button);
 const section=document.createElement('section');section.id='mastery';section.className='view';section.hidden=true;document.querySelector('main').appendChild(section);
 const key='statics-mastery-v1';let evidence={};try{evidence=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key)||'{}');}catch{}if(!evidence||typeof evidence!=='object'||Array.isArray(evidence))evidence={};
 function score(t){return MasteryMath.score(t.id,RoadmapData.problems,evidence);}
 function renderProgress(){let saved={};try{saved=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('statics-roadmap-v1')||'{}');}catch{}if(!saved||typeof saved!=='object'||Array.isArray(saved))saved={};const overall=Math.round(topics.reduce((s,t)=>s+score(t).percent,0)/topics.length);section.innerHTML=`<article class="panel"><h2>Independent application · ${overall}%</h2><progress max="100" value="${overall}" aria-label="Overall demonstrated mastery"></progress><p>Overall is the equal-weight average of the ${topics.length} topics currently included. A topic bar measures <strong>distinct problems completed correctly without hints or worked solutions during that attempt</strong>. Repeating the same problem does not add credit. This is evidence from this app, not a guarantee of exam readiness.</p><p>Reviewed solutions and assisted completions remain useful study; they do not count as independent demonstrations. Older completion checks are retained, but independent evidence begins with this update. Progress saves in this browser only.</p></article>${[2,3].map(ch=>`<article class="panel"><h2>Chapter ${ch}</h2><progress max="100" value="${Math.round(topics.filter(t=>t.chapter===ch).reduce((sum,t)=>sum+score(t).percent,0)/topics.filter(t=>t.chapter===ch).length)}" aria-label="Chapter ${ch} demonstrated mastery"></progress>${topics.filter(t=>t.chapter===ch).map(t=>{const s=score(t),studied=RoadmapData.problems.filter(p=>p.group===t.id&&saved[p.id]?.completed).length;return `<div class="mastery-topic"><strong>${t.title} · ${s.percent}%</strong><progress max="100" value="${s.percent}" aria-label="${esc(t.title)} independent mastery"></progress><p>${s.done}/${s.total} independent demonstrations · ${studied} walkthroughs completed, including assisted work</p><button data-progress-topic="${t.id}">Practise this topic →</button></div>`;}).join('')}</article>`).join('')}`;section.querySelectorAll('[data-progress-topic]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>GuidedRoadmap.open(b.dataset.progressTopic));const badge=$('overallMastery');if(badge)badge.textContent='Application progress: '+overall+'%';}
 const badge=document.createElement('button');badge.id='overallMastery';badge.onclick=()=>showView('mastery');document.querySelector('.study-sidebar').appendChild(badge);
 window.StudyMastery={record(p,state){if(MasteryMath.independent(p,state,RoadmapData.correct)){evidence[p.id]={at:Date.now()};try{localStorage.setItem(key,JSON.stringify(evidence));}catch{}}renderProgress();},render:renderProgress};renderProgress();
 const splash=document.createElement('dialog');splash.id='updateSplash';splash.setAttribute('aria-labelledby','updateSplashTitle');splash.innerHTML='<div class="panel-heading"><h2 id="updateSplashTitle">Fully updated</h2><button id="closeUpdateSplash" aria-label="Close update notice">×</button></div><p>Chapter navigation, topic and overall mastery bars, new Chapter 3 workspaces, integral foundations, and additional walkthroughs are now available.</p><p>All five supplied Exam 1 practice problems are included with their original diagrams and independently calculated solutions. This release covers the requested Chapter 2 and Chapter 3 expansion; mastery measures performance on the content currently in the app.</p>';document.body.appendChild(splash);$('closeUpdateSplash').onclick=()=>{splash.close();try{localStorage.setItem('statics-update-20261018-study','seen');}catch{}};try{if(!localStorage.getItem('statics-update-20261018-study')&&!window.examInProgress)splash.showModal();}catch{}
})();
